id:                     E396
trigger_tool:           conan|python|evidence-validator
phase:                  dependency-resolution|package-install|verification
error_signature:        package_folder.*null|package_folder.*missing|graph info.*package_folder

severity:               2
category:               conan, evidence, package-identity, schema
match_keywords:         Conan graph info, Conan install, package_folder null, RREV, PID, PREV, build never, isolated Conan home, package materialization
title:                  Bind Conan graph identity to install package materialization

root_cause:             Conan graph info resolves and serializes package identity but does not materialize a package for consumption, so a node may have complete RREV, PID, PREV, binary state, and remote attribution while package_folder is null. The successful install result for the same exact identity is the authoritative producer of the materialized package folder. Package inventory path fields are a separate schema and cannot substitute for package_folder.
affected_scope:         Conan 2 package validation that combines fresh OHOS/arm64 graph info and install --build=never results, then inspects artifacts or runs a package consumer.
verification_cmd:       Run graph info and install in one fresh isolated Conan home with identical profiles and --build=never; join the exact full ref/RREV/PID/PREV; allow graph package_folder=null; require install package_folder nonempty and verify artifacts below it.

rec_priority:           1
rec_approach:           cross-bind-graph-identity-and-install-folder
rec_description:        Use graph JSON for dependency topology, options, invalid/missing state, binary state, and remote attribution. Use install JSON for the materialized package_folder only after the exact node identity matches across both documents. Bind raw files, command RCs, isolated-home identity, and the derived result with SHA-256.
rec_command:            conan graph info <recipe> --build=never --format=json && conan install <recipe> --build=never --format=json
rec_auto_fix:           false
rec_impl:               evidence-validator

fallback_priority:      2
fallback_approach:      cache-path-readback-after-identity-join
fallback_description:   If a pinned Conan producer omits package_folder from install JSON too, query the same isolated cache only after binding the exact package reference and revisions; never guess a cache path.
fallback_command:
fallback_auto_fix:      false
fallback_impl:

forbid_1_pattern:       graph.*package_folder.*required|package_folder.*graph.*nonempty
forbid_1_reason:        graph info is not the package materialization command and can validly leave this field null.
forbid_1_consequence:   A complete successful run is falsely rejected and may be rerun unnecessarily.
forbid_2_pattern:       package_folder.*path|path.*package_folder|build=missing
forbid_2_reason:        Inventory path and Conan package_folder belong to different schemas, while build=missing destroys publication proof.
forbid_2_consequence:   The validator can inspect the wrong directory or accept a locally built provider.

principles:             P005,P010
causes:                 []
caused_by:              []
similar_to:             []
conflicts_with:         []
prerequisite_of:        []

